                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6a2dce53-882a-4f5f-aaf9-330a94dcfe84",
                        "source_entry_id": "53423210-c0d5-34aa-9f66-4fea8be9014b",
                        "source_sense_description": "испачкать кругом, со всех сторон",
                        "target_lang_word": "besmear",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "besmear",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab2898f6-b45e-38dc-aaa1-d060eeadfb43",
                                        "entry_id": "a435e108-7c36-3ddc-aa02-e5f2ebbf0a0a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To smear over, to smear all over, to daub."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca93bb18-11af-4fa9-b9a2-6fcabda327a9",
                                                "sense_id": "ab2898f6-b45e-38dc-aaa1-d060eeadfb43",
                                                "text": "I long to ſee thee backe returne from thence,\nThat I may view theſe milk-white ſteeds of mine.\nAll loden with the heads of killed men,\nAnd from their knees, euen to their hoofes below,\nBeſmer’d with blood, that makes a dainty ſhow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a052e2cf-f0df-478a-ba71-2f6c787527aa",
                                                "sense_id": "ab2898f6-b45e-38dc-aaa1-d060eeadfb43",
                                                "text": "[…] carters and coachmen, who make in imitation thereof a composition of grease and tar, with which they besmear the inside of the naves of wheels and the extremitys of the axis upon which they move."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "870c2433-595c-3300-8e80-517bbb374bd7",
                                        "entry_id": "a435e108-7c36-3ddc-aa02-e5f2ebbf0a0a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To damage the reputation of, to tarnish, to sully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c1c2004-e504-45bb-8754-1cf576d31408",
                                                "sense_id": "870c2433-595c-3300-8e80-517bbb374bd7",
                                                "text": "Novv, Sir, vvhen my Time comes, leſt they ſhou'd think it vvorth vvhile to handle my Memory vvith the ſame Freedom, I am vvilling to prevent its being ſo odly beſmear'd (or at beſt but flatly vvhite-vvash'd) by taking upon me to give the Publick This, as true a Picture of myſelf as natural Vanity vvill permit me to dravv; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "760a9365-aadf-42d1-bff3-9b8e4b99486c",
                                                "sense_id": "870c2433-595c-3300-8e80-517bbb374bd7",
                                                "text": "His public record is already besmeared with tawdry divorces, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "37f4624a-faa5-441e-8b84-0a6415871590",
                        "source_entry_id": "53423210-c0d5-34aa-9f66-4fea8be9014b",
                        "source_sense_description": "испачкать кругом, со всех сторон",
                        "target_lang_word": "soil",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "soil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a71e3956-2052-3fbf-b63d-62b20125e16a",
                                        "entry_id": "bea2dd25-224d-342f-b956-e6c546038f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mixture of mineral particles and organic material, used to support plant growth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d4d8fef-1a79-40e5-a496-332e9359ef6e",
                                                "sense_id": "a71e3956-2052-3fbf-b63d-62b20125e16a",
                                                "text": "We bought a bag of soil for the houseplants."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c993a9a6-6298-38aa-a2d9-ae5856e63f1e",
                                        "entry_id": "bea2dd25-224d-342f-b956-e6c546038f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The unconsolidated mineral or organic material on the immediate surface of the earth that serves as a natural medium for the growth of land plants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "609a760e-6afc-38bc-ba6c-8824b33094a0",
                                        "entry_id": "bea2dd25-224d-342f-b956-e6c546038f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The unconsolidated mineral or organic matter on the surface of the earth that has been subjected to and shows effects of genetic and environmental factors of: climate (including water and temperature effects), and macro- and microorganisms, conditioned by relief, acting on parent material over a period of time. A product-soil differs from the material from which it is derived in many physical, chemical, biological, and morphological properties and characteristics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ff0caf6-4cd4-3784-979c-77dd3b5bed44",
                                        "entry_id": "bea2dd25-224d-342f-b956-e6c546038f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Country or territory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62d2c0a6-d94b-4429-bff2-754ae794d127",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff0caf6-4cd4-3784-979c-77dd3b5bed44",
                                                "text": "Except during the season in town, she spends her year in golfing, either at St Magnus or Pau, for, like all good Americans, she has long since abjured her native soil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d64cd05-942d-469c-bf17-725e1d0b041c",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff0caf6-4cd4-3784-979c-77dd3b5bed44",
                                                "text": "Pro-democracy demonstrations in the Thai capital saw Germany's embassy become the focus Monday as the throngs of protesters gathered in front of the mission asked Berlin to investigate whether King Maha Vajiralongkorn is inappropriately conducting state business on German soil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c24250b-6477-3f0b-912b-88229d5fcc42",
                                        "entry_id": "bea2dd25-224d-342f-b956-e6c546038f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which soils or pollutes; a stain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "459f90e1-29de-4290-8fed-441388f9bb68",
                                                "sense_id": "0c24250b-6477-3f0b-912b-88229d5fcc42",
                                                "text": "And ſince not only a dead Fathers fame, / But more a Ladies honour muſt be touch’d, / Which nice as Ermines will not bear a Soil ; / Let all retire ; that you alone may hear / What ev’n in whiſpers I won’d tell your ear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "649db5e5-c1fb-3314-9211-f4313902bfd6",
                                        "entry_id": "bea2dd25-224d-342f-b956-e6c546038f63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A marshy or miry place to which a hunted boar resorts for refuge; hence, a wet place, stream, or tract of water, sought for by other game, as deer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0ca6163-a349-45d6-80f9-dac03c325517",
                                                "sense_id": "649db5e5-c1fb-3314-9211-f4313902bfd6",
                                                "text": "As Deere being ſtrucke flie thorow many ſoiles, / Yet ſtill the ſhaft ſitcks faſt, ſo ;"
